  "wiki": "Tehran",
  "summary": [
   "In the 1970s Tehran grew fast, to about four and a half million people, swollen by oil money and migrants from the countryside. The rich lived in the cool north, in the foothills of the Alborz. The poor crowded the south, near the bazaar and the old city.",
   "This plan shows the city as it was in 1978, with the names of the time and today's names in brackets: the great avenues of the marches, the squares where crowds gathered and were shot at, the palaces, the prisons, the airport and the embassy at the centre of the hostage crisis."
  ],
  "note": "Avenue lines follow today's streets (OSRM and OpenStreetMap). The university, Niavaran, Evin and the airport use OpenStreetMap outlines. The embassy compound, bazaar, Golestan Palace and Mosaddegh's house are drawn by hand and approximate.",
